      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2025-june/q8",
      "question": "<p>A rambler starts a walk at the bottom of a hill at 10 am.</p><p>The rambler walks all the way to the top of the hill and then turns around and walks back down to the bottom of the hill.</p><p>The differential equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sin t\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}-x\\cos t=A\\sin 2t\\sin t\\qquad t\\geqslant0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span data-math=\"A\"></span> is a constant, is used to model the vertical displacement, <span data-math=\"x\"></span> metres, of the rambler from the bottom of the hill, <span data-math=\"t\"></span> hours after the start of the walk.</p><p>Given that after 1 hour</p><ul><li>the rambler has a vertical displacement of 213 m</li><li><span data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}=273.2\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>determine the value of <span data-math=\"A\"></span> to 3 significant figures.</p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li><p>Hence, determine the particular solution of the differential equation, giving your answer in the form <span data-math=\"x=\\mathrm f(t)\"></span></p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li><p>Use the model to determine the time at which the rambler will return to the bottom of the hill.</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Given that the vertical displacement of the top of the hill is 300.68 m</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"4\"><li><p>use the model to find the value of <span data-math=\"t\"></span> when the rambler reaches the top of the hill.</p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li><p>Using your answers to parts (c) and (d), give a limitation of the model.</p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
