      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2025-june/q9",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li><p>The curves with equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac34\\sinh x\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=\\tanh x+\\frac15\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>intersect at just one point <span data-math=\"P\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Use algebra to show that the <span data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate of <span data-math=\"P\"></span> satisfies the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"15e^{4x}-48e^{3x}+32e^x-15=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li><p>Show that <span data-math=\"e^x=3\"></span> is a solution of this equation.</p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li><p>Hence state the exact coordinates of <span data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol></li><li><p>Show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_{-4}^{0}\\frac{e^{1/x}}{x^2}\\,\\mathrm dx=e^{-1/4}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
