      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Given that, for <span data-math=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\"></span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^n+\\frac1{z^n}=2\\cos n\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^n-\\frac1{z^n}=2i\\sin n\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"8\\sin^4\\theta\\equiv\\cos4\\theta-4\\cos2\\theta+3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol><figure class=\"practice-figure\"><img style=\"width:82mm;max-width:100%;height:auto\" src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9fm0-01-2025-june/q10-figures.png\" alt=\"Figures 1 and 2: the central vertical cross-section of a wooden ornament and the shaded region R between the curve and the y-axis, capped by a horizontal line.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows the central vertical cross-section of a solid wooden ornament.</p><p>Figure 2 shows the curve with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=\\sin^2\\left(\\frac12y\\right)\\qquad0\\leqslant y\\leqslant\\frac{8\\pi}{5}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The region <span data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 2, is bounded by the curve, the line with equation <span data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{8\\pi}{5}\"></span> and the <span data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis.</p><p>The ornament is modelled by the solid of revolution formed when <span data-math=\"R\"></span> is rotated <span data-math=\"360^\\circ\"></span> about the <span data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis. The units are centimetres.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Using algebraic integration and the result in part (a), determine, in <span data-math=\"\\mathrm{cm}^3\"></span>, the volume of wood needed to make the ornament, according to the model. Give your answer to 2 significant figures.</p><p><em>[Solutions based entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.]</em></p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol><p>Given that</p><ul><li>the density of the wood is <span data-math=\"0.85\\ \\mathrm{g/cm}^3\"></span></li><li>the mass of the ornament is 6 grams</li></ul><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"3\"><li><p>comment on the suitability of the model.</p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
